  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale-up learnings on RBC among different sectors in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to improve working and employment conditions in the textiles, garment, leather and natural stone supply chains in India. The project will work towards this objective through a two-pronged approach:&#x2022;	Scaling up and expanding successful interventions of the factory support programme in the garment industry. Arisa  will replicate successful approaches with other companies within the garment industry and across sectors (the natural stone sector and the leather sector) by sharing experiences and lessons from previous  projects.  Furthermore, with a selected number of frontrunner companies the project would lilke to take the next steps towards social dialogue, freedom of association and living wages; and&#x2022;	Promoting and strengthening meaningful engagement between importers and suppliers as well as with rights-holders and (civil society) stakeholders on responsible business conduct (RBC) issues. Meaningful engagement can cover a variety of RBC topics. For Arisa and its partners key issues include forced labour, child labour and discrimination.</narrative>
  </description>
